# Host build artefacts. `.venv` is the one that bites: uv writes a venv whose
# bin/python symlinks to an interpreter path that exists on the host and not
# in the image, so copying it in doesn't just waste layers — `uv run` inside
# the container finds it, declares it linked to a non-existent interpreter,
# deletes it, and re-resolves the whole dependency tree from PyPI at *start*
# time. That turned a transient pythonhosted timeout into `souk-migrate`
# exiting 1 and taking the stack down with it.
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[co]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
# The local SQLite database a dev run leaves behind (souk/souk.db). Baking
# one into the image means a container can silently come up against it.
**/*.db

# Hermes Agent's own runtime data directory (providers/openai-compat-agent/
# hermes-data, bind-mounted into the `hermes` demo container) — never
# needed inside any image we build, and its files end up owned by the
# container's internal uid (10000), which can make it unreadable to the
# Docker build context depending on host permissions.
providers/openai-compat-agent/hermes-data
